Z||000000||DXR_DAD||05-23-2000||08:02 PM||||George Can you Post the Time, Date, and Info fo the Poker Run?  Cliff had the upcoming event section, it's not there. Some of the guys & gals might want to make the trip.<BR>I know that Bruce is close to us and close<BR>to being a Golden Gate Fiero Member???<P>Fun! Fun! Fun! and mo Fun!!!! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">:<P>Al, from down LA way might want to make it<BR>and bring some of that South Cali Sun?<P>Thanks<BR>DXR_DAD||||reg||1
Z||000001||fieroshop||05-24-2000||12:56 AM||||The poker run will be held on Sunday June 11th. There will be a barbecue following the run. The run will start at 9:30 AM with singups at 9:00 AM. This year the run will be aprox. 75 miles with more then half being in the country with narrow roads and plenty of curves. There will be four checkpoints to find and at each point the driver draws a card and so does the passenger. No you can't mix the cards together as the driver draws a blue card and the passenger a red card. There will be a small car show and this year there will be six trophies. This is what the trophies look, as you notice there is a spot to put a plaque describing what the win was for.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Trophy_1.JPG">   <BR>There will be door prizes and a raffle and prizes for the top three hands. Don't forget the barbecue. This event is getting bigger and better each year. This is a not to miss event.<BR>Some of you might remember where tgowens wrote about his GT and said that I kept his old dogbone for a trophy. Well this is what I do with them.<BR>If any of you have an old dogbone I would like to get it so that I could make more tropies with them.<P><p>[This message has been edited by fieroshop (edited 05-24-2000).]||||reg||1
